    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "bd415148-0f41-3ad5-b5ee-6c3d291cf798",
                "word": "coincident",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f856305d-af65-4624-b8ee-be05b0c32f4d",
                        "entry_id": "bd415148-0f41-3ad5-b5ee-6c3d291cf798",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more coincident"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "51b59594-9ef2-40ab-a8ba-e80058051eb2",
                        "entry_id": "bd415148-0f41-3ad5-b5ee-6c3d291cf798",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most coincident"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b4651855-a8c2-30cb-a142-110acd072fed",
                        "entry_id": "bd415148-0f41-3ad5-b5ee-6c3d291cf798",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of two or more objects: being in the same location."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8594beee-67b8-4289-ba06-686ee481f170",
                                "sense_id": "b4651855-a8c2-30cb-a142-110acd072fed",
                                "text": "It is neceſſary therefore that this nevv created or replaced thing do not onely fill ſome part of the Space [i.e. “imaginary space”] above-mentioned, or be coincident and coextended vvith it, but alſo, that it have no dependance upon our thought."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d035424f-4d3f-409b-b957-db56e4eac427",
                                "sense_id": "b4651855-a8c2-30cb-a142-110acd072fed",
                                "text": "[T]he ſides of the angles A and D are coincident; vvherefore thoſe angles are equall. VVhich vvas to be Dem[onstrated]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ea5fc15-a0ff-44d7-bbbc-70bf7df036a7",
                                "sense_id": "b4651855-a8c2-30cb-a142-110acd072fed",
                                "text": "[A]ll the Colours of the ſame Ring muſt be coincident, and by their mixture exhibit a vvhite Ring."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ada6d1e3-1020-41a3-b948-e6adeec3c837",
                                "sense_id": "b4651855-a8c2-30cb-a142-110acd072fed",
                                "text": "Hitherto, the Universe of stars has always been considered as coincident with the Universe proper, as I have defined it in the commencement of this Discourse. It has always been either directly or indirectly assumed—at least since the dawn of intelligible Astronomy—that, were it possible for us to attain any given point in space, we should still find, on all sides of us, an interminable succession of stars."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2217f833-da06-438a-aafd-60e1580d755f",
                                "sense_id": "b4651855-a8c2-30cb-a142-110acd072fed",
                                "text": "On each soft side [of the White Whale]—coincident with the parted swell, that but once leaving him, then flowed so wide away—on each bright side, the whale shed off enticings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e0d9908-c3ef-423f-b0c6-da3823d32d03",
                                "sense_id": "b4651855-a8c2-30cb-a142-110acd072fed",
                                "text": "The primary cause of the ocean currents, and of the prevailing winds which are associated with them, is the rotation of the earth. The plot of the Atlantic currents and Atlantic winds is almost, though not quite, coincident."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8f025cce-e938-3be1-920d-7463fd998aa5",
                        "entry_id": "bd415148-0f41-3ad5-b5ee-6c3d291cf798",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of two or more events: occurring at the same time; contemporaneous."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "19eab496-223a-4ff3-8600-e6c9ea96240d",
                                "sense_id": "8f025cce-e938-3be1-920d-7463fd998aa5",
                                "text": "The 13th year of his [Darius II's] Reign vvas coincident in vvinter vvith the 20th of the Peloponneſian vvar, and the years of that vvar are ſtated by indiſputable characters, and agreed on by all Chronologers: the vvar began in ſpring, Ann[o] 1. Olymp[iad] 87, laſted 27 years, and ended Apr. 14. An. 4. Olymp. 93."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9264186-d5f0-4da2-a089-7f3ff20934dd",
                                "sense_id": "8f025cce-e938-3be1-920d-7463fd998aa5",
                                "text": "Whatever the origin of her walks on the Budmouth Road, her return from those walks was often coincident with Farfrae's emergence from Corn Street for a twenty minutes' blow on that rather windy highway―just to winnow the seeds and chaff out of him before sitting down to tea, as he said."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c21942d-ddb4-4e65-a49c-999028d21257",
                                "sense_id": "8f025cce-e938-3be1-920d-7463fd998aa5",
                                "text": "General trends, like the coincident decline of the nation-state and the growth of antisemitism, can hardly ever be explained satisfactorily by one reason or by one cause alone."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6bbf8d6-3dc5-4620-9f34-29e734d912a3",
                                "sense_id": "8f025cce-e938-3be1-920d-7463fd998aa5",
                                "text": "Duverger's health declined. He seemed unable to shake the bronchitis and the coincident infections it opened him to."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f96c109c-7081-316c-b31e-e29961de45d4",
                        "entry_id": "bd415148-0f41-3ad5-b5ee-6c3d291cf798",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of two or more things: having the same qualities; being in accordance; consonant, matching."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "85d11afd-75ab-42de-8a2a-4b4c85649f86",
                                "sense_id": "f96c109c-7081-316c-b31e-e29961de45d4",
                                "text": "[A] biſhop is he to whomſoeuer the publike cure and charge of ſoules is committed, without any limitation of place. And ſo the name of biſhop is coincident with the office of apoſtle, or any publike paſtor, doctor, or curat of the vniuerſall flocke of Chriſt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25540499-152b-4830-bb71-95bb002e3ed3",
                                "sense_id": "f96c109c-7081-316c-b31e-e29961de45d4",
                                "text": "For, say they, the whole doctrine of Christianity teaches nothing but what is perfectly suitable to, and coincident with, the ruling principles; that a virtuous and well-inclined man is acted by and with the main interest that he proposes to himself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9aef16e2-a05a-4856-95f4-f087b9a3fa87",
                                "sense_id": "f96c109c-7081-316c-b31e-e29961de45d4",
                                "text": "As to any other laws that slave-holders may make among themselves, as respecting slaves, they can be of no better kind, nor give them any better character, than what is implied in the common report—that there may be some honesty among thieves. This may seem a harsh comparison, but the parallel is so coincident that, I must say, I can find no other way of expressing my Thoughts and Sentiments, without making use of some harsh words and comparisons against the carriers on of such abandoned wickedness."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4e156177-7d73-36a2-8f77-7568ae04b6ae",
                        "entry_id": "bd415148-0f41-3ad5-b5ee-6c3d291cf798",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chiefly followed by to: accompanying, concomitant, incident."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d42a11b6-f26f-47ec-9d66-bced3b2419ae",
                                "sense_id": "4e156177-7d73-36a2-8f77-7568ae04b6ae",
                                "text": "Empires of Kings, are novv, and ever vvere / As Saluſt ſaith, co-incident to feare."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
